jt-pve-storage-synology (0.1.1~beta1-1) unstable; urgency=low

  * The snapshot restore method is named restore_snapshot, established against
    hardware. Nine candidate names were asked about; one answered. Rollback is
    still refused in this release: knowing a method exists is not knowing its
    parameters or whether it keeps newer snapshots and preserves the LUN uuid.
  * The LUN listing no longer sends a types filter. Synology's own CSI driver
    sends an explicit twelve-type list, and on the test NAS that list hid a
    Virtual Machine Manager virtual disk whose 120 GiB comes out of the same
    volume. The probe now lists unfiltered and reports what the filter would
    have hidden.
  * The register no longer reports a listing that was skipped as one the
    account could not read. Skipped, refused and succeeded are three different
    outcomes, and conflating the first two is the mistake this project's own
    rules exist to prevent.
  * A read method that succeeds is no longer flagged as alarming; only a
    destructive candidate succeeding is.
  * Error 18990004 recorded, observed from SYNO.Core.ISCSI.Host get.

 -- Jason Cheng (Jason Tools) <jason@jason.tools>  Thu, 06 Aug 2026 15:00:00 +0800

jt-pve-storage-synology (0.1.0~beta1-1) unstable; urgency=low

  * First packaged build. Contains no storage plugin.
  * pve-syno-api-probe: read-only discovery of a Synology DSM's SAN Web API.
    Discovers API paths and version ranges rather than hardcoding them, carries
    a session both ways because the two public reference clients disagree about
    which works, echoes the anti-CSRF token neither of them sends, and never
    puts a credential in a URL.
  * docs/TESTING.md: the register of what is verified against hardware and what
    is not, with the test plan for closing the gap.
  * docs/DSM-ACCOUNT.md: the DSM account the plugin needs, what can be taken
    away from it, and the Auto Block behaviour that makes retrying a rejected
    credential dangerous.

 -- Jason Cheng (Jason Tools) <jason@jason.tools>  Thu, 06 Aug 2026 12:00:00 +0800
